            "body": "Modern development setups demand efficiency and minimal clutter. A monitor equipped with single-cable USB-C docking is a game-changer. This feature allows a single USB-C cable to simultaneously: \n\n*   Transmit high-resolution video and audio from your laptop to the monitor (via DisplayPort Alt Mode).\n*   Deliver up to 90W of power, charging most modern laptops without needing a separate power brick.\n*   Enable data transfer for connected peripherals through the monitor's integrated USB hub (e.g., keyboard, mouse, webcam, external drives).\n*   Crucially, provide a stable, fast wired network connection via an integrated RJ45 Ethernet port. This eliminates reliance on potentially less reliable Wi-Fi and ensures robust connectivity essential for large code repository clones, frequent data transfers, and seamless integration with corporate networks. \n\nThis architecture simplifies cable management, frees up laptop ports, and makes connecting or disconnecting your workstation effortless."
